.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ttychatter.bash
is the Bash-only, dependency-light ttychatter edition. It keeps plain text logs,
model selection, simple attachment extraction, session listing, title metadata,
search, and batch/interactive command-line use available on older systems.
.PP
This edition intentionally scales down some advanced features. It supports
log renaming, branch creation, turns display, simple export, external voice
hooks, and local status updates. It does not implement edit-and-branch or JSON
export; use the C edition or ttychatter.python for those.
.SH SESSION LOGS
New logs begin with:
.PP
.nf
Everyone is encouraged to get the cruelty-free vegetarian alternatives and remember the bloodguilt curse from the Bible... http://bloodguiltcurse.net
.fi
.PP
Logs are stored under
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
or, when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset,
.IR ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions .
Unnamed logs start with timestamped filenames. PROMPT_SESSION_NAME=1 (default)
prominently asks for a name when an interactive unnamed session is opened.
Enter defers naming. Batch and piped input never block on a naming prompt.
.PP
:rename and --rename-session update the actual filename and session-title
metadata. The filename is TITLE--ID.log: an ASCII title slug of at most 80
characters plus the first 12 characters of a stable 32-character session ID.
Collisions receive a numeric suffix without overwriting another log. Manual
titles preserve up to 200 characters independently of SESSION_TITLE_MAX_WORDS.
Existing files can be opened without conversion. --list shows friendly names
and real filenames. The current human title and recorded previous titles or
filename stems can also resume, export, or manage renamed sessions. An exact
existing filename takes priority; ambiguous title or alias matches require
choosing a filename from --list. Alias searches skip symbolic links.
.PP
--output remains fixed during automatic naming; explicit rename commands may
rename it within its directory. Symlink paths are not renamed. Renaming requires
ln with -T support and filesystem hard links; failures preserve the source.
New logs are private to the current user. The final stderr marker after a
request, and stdout marker after --rename-session, is session: followed by the
absolute current log path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show built-in help.
.TP
.B --version
Show version information.
.TP
.B --demo
Use local demo responses instead of live OpenRouter requests.
.TP
.BR -i , " --interactive"
Force interactive mode.
.TP
.BR -n , " --new"
Create a fresh timestamped session and reject accidental session/output operands.
.TP
.BR -p , " --prompt " TEXT
Send TEXT once and save the exchange.
.TP
.BR --input " FILE"
Read a one-shot prompt from FILE. Use - for standard input.
.TP
.BR -o , " --output " FILE
Write the session log to FILE for the current batch/chat invocation.
.TP
.BR -s , " --session " SESSION
Use SESSION as the active session name or path.
.TP
.B --list
List saved sessions, showing session-title metadata when present.
.TP
.BR --rename-session " SESSION TITLE"
Set the friendly title and safely rename the actual log file.
.TP
.BR --search " QUERY"
Search saved session logs. With no active session, searches all saved sessions.
.TP
.B --all-sessions
Use with --search to search all sessions.
.TP
.BR --turns " SESSION"
List user/assistant message numbers in SESSION.
.TP
.BR --branch " SESSION TURN"
Create an independently identified, named branch containing messages through TURN.
.TP
.BR --edit-turn " SESSION TURN"
Recognized but not implemented in the Bash-only edition.
.TP
.BR --export " SESSION"
Export SESSION. Use --format markdown or --format text.
Multiline messages and code fences are preserved; internal metadata is omitted.
An output-file write failure returns a nonzero status.
.TP
.BR --format " markdown|text"
Choose export format.
.TP
.BR --models
List models using live/cache metadata.
.TP
.B --routers
List router/special model entries.
.TP
.BR --model-type " all|routers|fixed|free|auto"
Filter model display.
.TP
.BR --sort " name|input-tokens|output-tokens|type|favorites"
Sort model display when supported by the cache parser.
.TP
.BR --min-input-tokens " N"
Show only models with at least N input/context tokens when metadata is available.
.TP
.BR --min-output-tokens " N"
Show only models with at least N output tokens when metadata is available.
.TP
.B --show-preview | --hide-preview
Control model preview display when model metadata is available.
.TP
.B --require-tokens
Hide model rows that lack token-limit metadata.
.TP
.B --allow-missing-tokens
Allow model rows that lack token-limit metadata.
.TP
.B --update-models
Refresh the model cache.
.TP
.BR --test-model " MODEL"
Test one model with MODEL_TEST_PROMPT.
.TP
.B --select-model
Open a numbered model selector.
.TP
.B --save
With --test-model or --select-model, persist a successful model selection.
.TP
.B --favorites
List favorite models.
.TP
.BR --favorite-model " MODEL"
Bookmark MODEL.
.TP
.BR --unfavorite-model " MODEL"
Remove MODEL from bookmarks.
.TP
.BR --unbookmark-model " MODEL"
Alias for --unfavorite-model.
.TP
.B --config
Print config summary.
.TP
.BR --set " KEY VALUE"
Save a config key.
.TP
.BR --unset " KEY"
Remove a config key.
.TP
.B --set-api-key
Prompt for an API key and offer runtime-only, gpg-encrypted, or plaintext config storage.
.TP
.B --forget-api-key
Remove plaintext API-key config entries.
.TP
.BR --attach " FILE"
Attach FILE to the next model request.
.TP
.BR --theme " THEME"
Set the runtime theme variable for parity with other editions.
.TP
.BR --send-input " MODE"
Set input sending mode, such as ctrl_d or enter.
.TP
.BR --code-attachment-min-lines " N"
Minimum fenced-code lines before generated code is saved as an attachment.
.TP
.BR --stream , " --no-stream"
Enable or disable real-time streamed assistant output. Press ESC during an active stream to stop it; the partial reply is saved with an interruption marker.
.TP
.BR --web , " --no-web"
Enable or disable the OpenRouter web-search server tool. The default is off.
The model decides when to search. Sources are appended to the answer and log.
.TP
.BR --web-engine " ENGINE"
Select auto, native, exa, parallel, perplexity, or firecrawl. Default: auto.
.TP
.BR --web-max-results " N"
Set results per search, from 0 to 25 (default 5). Zero leaves the provider default. Perplexity is capped at 20 when nonzero.
.TP
.BR --web-max-uses " N"
Set search rounds from 0 to 25 (default 3). Zero omits ttychatter's max_tool_calls cap.
.TP
.BR --ai-download " ask|auto|metadata|off"
Control provider-returned file attachments. ask prompts before saving when possible and records metadata in batch use. auto saves all returned files under ATTACHMENT_DIR/received, metadata lists them without saving, and off ignores them. The Bash-only edition requires jq for structured returned-file detection.
.TP
.BR --status , " --progress"
Print local progress/status notes to stderr.
.TP
.BR --no-status , " --no-progress"
Disable local progress/status notes.
.TP
.BR --voice-input " FILE"
Transcribe FILE with VOICE_INPUT_CMD and send the resulting text.
.TP
.BR --transcribe " FILE"
Transcribe FILE with VOICE_INPUT_CMD.
.TP
.B --speak
Send assistant output to VOICE_OUTPUT_CMD or TTS_CMD.
.TP
.B --no-speak
Disable voice output.
.TP
.B --doctor
Run diagnostics.
.TP
.B --credits
Show project credits.
.TP
.B --resume SESSION
Resume an existing session.
.TP
.B --loopback
Route interface text to stderr and model output to stdout.
.TP
.BR --loopback-file " PATH"
Append each model output to PATH.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The shared config file is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/config
or, when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset,
.IR ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config .
Sessions default to
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions ,
attachments to
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments ,
and the model cache to
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json .
Model favorites default to
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/model-favorites .
All implementations use these shared paths and still read the old
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/config
file as a compatibility fallback when the provider-specific config is absent.
Relevant parity keys include MODEL, CONTEXT_TURNS, SESSION_DIR, ATTACHMENT_DIR,
STARTUP_NOTICE, SESSION_AUTO_TITLE, SESSION_TITLE_MODEL,
SESSION_TITLE_MAX_WORDS, PROMPT_SESSION_NAME, WEB_SEARCH, WEB_SEARCH_ENGINE,
WEB_SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS, WEB_SEARCH_MAX_USES, STREAM, AI_FILE_DOWNLOAD_MODE, STATUS_UPDATES, VOICE_INPUT_CMD,
VOICE_OUTPUT_CMD, TTS_CMD, VOICE_OUTPUT, MODEL_CACHE_FILE,
MODEL_FAVORITES_FILE, SEND_INPUT, and CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES.
.PP
SESSION_AUTO_TITLE defaults to 0. When enabled, ttychatter may use
SESSION_TITLE_MODEL as a secondary model only for a title and corresponding
managed filename. Title generation never requests web search.
.PP
Session memory restores the latest complete JSON or legacy text snapshot, then
replays newer messages. Explicit memory edits and empty snapshots are preserved.
New snapshots use JSON so embedded newlines and role-looking text remain exact.
.SH RUNTIME COMMANDS
Interactive commands begin with a colon. Supported commands include :help,
:rename TITLE, :turns, :branch N, :search TEXT, :search-all TEXT, :web [on|off|status], :stream on|off,
:ai-download MODE, :status on|off, :voice FILE, :speak on|off|last, :models, :favorites,
:select-model, :config, :memory, :attach FILE, :editor, and :credits.
.SH WEB SEARCH AND RESPONSE HANDLING
WEB_SEARCH=0 is the default. --web and :web on enable OpenRouter's current
openrouter:web_search server tool; :web shows its current state.
The deprecated web plugin and model :online suffix are not used automatically.
Searches may add provider charges. The result and use settings are bounds sent
to the provider, not a strict cost cap; native search may ignore some limits.
The request caps tool calls at five and total search results at fifteen. No local command execution is delegated to the model.
.PP
Sources remain human-readable in responses and session logs, including streamed
annotation events after text has ended. Available usage, response identifiers,
and annotations are also saved as system: openrouter-response: JSON metadata.
Session IDs are opaque and stable across title changes; titles and local paths
are not sent as request identifiers.
.PP
Streaming runs until [DONE], retains newline-only deltas and final usage, and
preserves partial output when stopped with ESC. API and transport errors are
reported as failures, never inserted into memory as assistant claims. Batch
commands return a nonzero status on failure. No automatic paid retries occur. If a reply has arrived but log or code-file
saving fails, its original text stays visible and the command reports failure.
Extracted code files use exclusive creation so previous replies are not overwritten.
.PP
Web search and lossless streaming require jq. Basic buffered chat still works
without jq using the documented best-effort JSON response parser. Requesting
streaming without jq falls back to a single buffered request. Requesting web
search without jq fails before sending a request. Resuming a session containing
JSON memory snapshots also requires jq; the client refuses to silently bypass
intentional memory edits or clearing. Without jq it reads/writes legacy text
snapshots for basic local chat.
.SH SEE ALSO
ttychatter.python(1), ttychatter.ncurses(1)
